      "id": "css-tables-3.rowspan-kept-row-footer-output",
      "source_id": "css-tables-3",
      "sections": [
        "breaking-rules"
      ],
      "behaviour": "The repeated footer precedes unused space after a kept row break. Each row is 14pt line height + 8pt padding + 0.5pt collapsed border = 22.5pt. The table starts at 10.25pt, and the footer follows one header and three body rows on pages 1 and 2, or two body rows on page 3. Its glyph baseline adds 4.25pt padding/border plus 7 + (1901-483)*10/(2*2048) from the locked font hhea metrics. PDF y is 140 minus that baseline. Only F is selected; spanning-cell alignment is not assumed by this assertion.",
      "applicability": {
        "status": "applicable",
        "reason": "Static paginated tables with repeated footers and spanning cells."
      },
      "dependencies": [],
      "implementation": {
        "status": "unknown",
        "evidence": []
      },
      "case_ids": [
        "rowspan-kept-row-footer"
      ],
      "priority": "foundations",
      "review_state": "reviewed",
      "verification": [
        {
          "case_id": "rowspan-kept-row-footer",
          "assertion_id": "footer-origins"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "css-inline-3.explicit-fallback-line-height-output",
      "source_id": "css-inline-3",
      "sections": [
        "inline-height"
      ],
      "behaviour": "CSS Inline 3 inline-height uses only the first available font for non-normal layout bounds. STIX hhea ascent 1055 and descent -455 at 1000 units/em yield a 10pt baseline offset for 10pt/14pt text. Three 14pt lines start at page y=10pt; PDF marker baselines are 80, 66 and 52pt. Fallback glyphs must not enlarge those lines, including in a child span. CSS Inline 3 inline-height includes all glyph metrics for normal layout bounds. U+214A is absent from DejaVu Sans and present in STIX. Its 10.55pt ascent and 4.55pt descent exceed the first font metrics; after the three fixed 14pt lines the baseline is 10+42+10.55pt from the page top, or PDF y=37.45pt.",
      "applicability": {
        "status": "applicable",
        "reason": "Horizontal inline layout with explicit and normal line heights and font fallback."
      },
      "dependencies": [],
      "implementation": {
        "status": "unknown",
        "evidence": []
      },
      "case_ids": [
        "fallback-explicit-line-height"
      ],
      "priority": "foundations",
      "review_state": "reviewed",
      "verification": [
        {
          "case_id": "fallback-explicit-line-height",
          "assertion_id": "fixed-baselines"
        },
        {
          "case_id": "fallback-explicit-line-height",
          "assertion_id": "normal-fallback"
        }
      ]
    },
